From e6c28ab198b2ca8c46618b810bcfcc92cc1b483c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jan 2025 16:14:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1473/1695] dts: stm32: move scmi-server configuration in a
 separate file

Move SCMI server (based on SCP) configuration for STMicroelectronics
boards in a separate file "stm32mp25-st-scmi-cfg.dtsi", because
this configuration is not SoC generic but board specific.

This files can be reused by others boards or copied and customized
for specific needs.

Moreover this file prepare the CM33TDCID support as SCMI server
configuration is not required CM33TDCID.

This patch also reorders the "domain-name" element in STM32MP21
device treee to allow comparition with STM32MP23/25 files.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 82fdaf0bf6afba599daa913733e45c0866122cee dts: stm32: move scmi-server configuration in a separate file]
Change-Id: Ia98b68005964c385df25896e53a92235a0b4b55d
Signed-off-by: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/429882
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
